# === eCash Live .gitignore ===
# This IS the real repo (github.com/tuannato/eCash-Live, remote `origin`).
# Everything below is either a secret, a private working note, a runtime
# artifact, or a regenerable file. See CLAUDE.md §14.

# --- Private working material (NEVER commit) ---
# internal/ holds design docs, review artifacts, workplans, logo source files,
# sampler output, and at least one script with a live API token in it. None of
# it is part of the published site. Both forms on purpose: the bare name also
# catches a SYMLINK named `internal` (the exact way a committed node_modules
# symlink once broke the Pages build — see the Worker section below).
internal
internal/

# --- Secrets (NEVER commit) ---
.env
*.env
ecash_bot_config.json
.ecash_bot_config.json
*ecash_bot_config*
*.config.json
ecash_bot.py
# Generic credential shapes, so a new file cannot slip through by being named
# something we did not predict.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
*secret*
*credentials*
*.token
.netrc
.npmrc

# --- Relay runtime artifacts (regenerated on the VPS) ---
ttf-stats.json
ttf.log
ttf-daily.jsonl
ttf-stats.json.tmp
ws-traffic.log

# --- Generated navigation map (regenerable via project-index.py) ---
PROJECT_INDEX.md

# --- Local backups (safety net for this offline copy — never committed) ---
*.bak
*.bak.*

# --- Local-only tooling (not part of the site) ---
.claude/launch.json
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.md

# --- Worker toolchain (P3 Stage 1) ---
# wrangler + its deps are ~206MB and are reinstalled by `npm ci` from the
# committed package-lock.json. The lockfile IS committed so deploys are
# reproducible; node_modules never is. The Worker source itself (src/,
# wrangler.toml, package.json) is part of the repo.
# NO trailing slash on purpose. `node_modules/` matches only DIRECTORIES, so a
# SYMLINK named node_modules slips through and gets committed — which broke the
# GitHub Pages build (Jekyll followed the link, the target does not exist in the
# repo, Errno::ENOENT). Without the slash both are ignored.
node_modules
.wrangler

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
